
REDOffline - RED Offline Package
=========================================================

This is REDOffline, data processing package in RED collaboration. 
It is created to analyse scintific data in the form of waveforms of 
signals from real detector.

This software is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but
'AS IS', without any warrany, expressed or implied, of any kind, 
even merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose.

Full information on REDOffline is available on the web:

    http://enpl.mephi.ru/twiki/bin/view.pl/Main/RedOffline

Installation
============

Prerequisities:
    cmake >= 2.8
    ROOT >= 5.34
    C++ compiler (gcc >=4.0)
    make

The current stable version of REDOffline is available from
  https://lab344.mephi.ru/Current Activity/Software/REDOffline/REDOffline-latest.tar.bz2
Just download archive file and unpack it to a suitable directory.

A development version can be acquired from git repository
  git clone ssh://<you>@lab344.mephi.ru/home/git/REDOffline.git/

In both cases you will get a tree of source files of the project.
Compile it with usual commands:
  $ mkdir build && cd build
  $ cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<your_path> ..
  $ make install

NB: If you want to use non-standard options or directories you can provide it to
cmake using environment values or cmake command arguments.

Usage
=====

Main program executable is called 'offline'. It is run as

  $ ./offline -I 'input_module' -c config_file -o output_file <input_files> [-n max_events] [-i]

Program will sequentially open input files, read and process events from there
and write resulting events to output file. It can read data files of various
types, but if file type is other than standard File, one must provide a valid
class name for proper input module.

Full list of command-line options is printed using '-h' option.
